    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="29b46d2d-8332-542b-99a4-38a5b6113c3a" activityNameId="aa555216-4dff-573d-8327-ec520ecc85d4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sugar refinery</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sugar refinery
Sugar refinery with a production capacity of 200 kt sugar per year (production period of 100-180 days/year, depending on the feedstock). Life time is taken as 50 years. Equivalent feed capacities vary from 1’300 kt/yr for sugar beets to 1’650 kt/yr for sugarcane.;
UUID: c397af8b-c383-3730-86b5-79eaaf77789a
This process includes land use and occupation, buildings and facilities of a typical sugar refinery in the global context. Energy use for construction and related emissions and/or waste effluents are not included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Technology is of a standard sugar refinery, including washing of the feedstock, juice extraction, purification and crystallisation. Juice extraction is performed by diffusion. 
Time period: undefined
Production volume: World production of sugar was 130 Mt in 2000
Sampling: Data was adapted from the ethanol fermentation plant dataset. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_c397af8b-c383-3730-86b5-79eaaf77789a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
